<title>MALAYSIA: MBM Resources asks for stock suspension.</title>
<headline>MBM Resources asks for stock suspension.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vehicle distributor and parts maker MBM Resources Bhd said it was asking for the suspension of its shares from Monday pending a news announcement.</p>
<p>The company did not give any other details in its one-paragraph statement to the Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>MBM is the sole distributor of Japanese-made Daihatsu vehicles in Malaysia through 71.5 percent Daihatsu (Malaysia) Sdn Bhd, which is also a Perodua dealer.</p>
<p>MBM stock was last traded at 5.85 ringgit on Friday.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newroom (603-201 4813)</p>
</text>
